    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20061128.0451\n\nMEXICO CITY, Nov. 28 , 2006 (Xinhua)\n\nStocks close higher in Argentina, Brazil, lower in Mexico\n\n\n\n\nLatin America's three major stock markets closed mixed on Tuesday.\n\nThe Buenos Aires stock market closed with the Merval index up 0.81 percent at 1,907.57 points. The trade volume was 16.451 million dollars.\n\nIn Sao Paulo, Latin America's biggest bourse, the leading Bovespa index closed at 41,043 points, up 0.31 percent. The trade volume was 983 million dollars.\n\nMexico City's IPC stock index drooped by 0.4 percent to close at 24,344.95 points. A total of 140.8 million shares were traded at 398.9 million U.S. dollars.",
